  "_comment": [
    "Regression baseline for the challenge suite (SyntheticRGBD --suite",
    "challenge, fixture challenge.ldr, seed 7), checked by",
    "Tools/RecoveryEvaluation/check_regression.py. Kept apart from the",
    "real-tower baseline so adding mistake classes never moves it.",
    "",
    "These counts record what the verifier gets wrong today, on purpose:",
    "- plate_up1: a brick one plate (3.2 mm) too high reads COMPLETE on",
    "  every strongly detectable step. The 6 mm depth tolerance swallows",
    "  the offset. This is a real false-complete class, not an expected",
    "  failure. The build diff tallies a +-1 plate contest on every",
    "  placement and by design never acts on it (ADR 0008 amendment). Read",
    "  through score_results.py (VERTICAL_CONTEST, 2026-10-08), the raised",
    "  contest is decisive on 3/3 strong plate_up1 rows and on 0/7 strong",
    "  controls, though two target rows carry only 36-38 contested pixels",
    "  against the 30 floor. The candidate fix is a block-only vertical",
    "  contest, which may take a complete away and never concludes an",
    "  offset; it needs an ADR 0008 amendment and waits for device windows",
    "  (NEXT_STEPS 1a item 16).",
    "- colour_swap: expected failure. Depth cannot see colour; the RGB",
    "  support term (ADR 0008) is what flips it.",
    "Per-class cases are guarded exactly and false completes as",
    "lower_is_better, so a fix shows as an improvement and any change in",
    "which rows exist fails loudly.",
    "",
    "Guards added by hand (2026-10-08), because --update adds only counts:",
    "the geometrically correct controls stay complete. A plate contest that",
    "over-blocks would otherwise pass this file: it would lower",
    "colour_swap.false_complete_cases and read as an improvement. So",
    "rot90/rot180_symmetric correct_complete, colour_swap produced.complete",
    "and the diff's present.present are higher_is_better. Later --update",
    "runs keep them and refresh their values.",
    "",
    "Regenerate with --update and explain the movement in the commit message."
  ],
